{"arrivo":"nl","origine":"de","origine_nome":"German","livello2":"grc","livello2_nome":"Ancient Greek","n":16,"parole":[{"parola":"axiologie","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"perhaps","significato":"axiology","termine_origine":"Axiologie","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Axiologie","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"ἄξιος","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Perhaps borrowed from German Axiologie. Ultimately from Ancient Greek ἄξιος (áxios, “worthy”)."},{"parola":"biologie","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"biology (science of living matter)","termine_origine":"Biologie","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Biologie","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"βιολογία","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from German Biologie, from Ancient Greek βιολογία (biología). This is a compound of βίος (bíos, “life”) and λόγος (lógos, “reason”) with the suffix -ία (-ía) (forms abstracta), equivalent to bio- + -logie."},{"parola":"dynamiet","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly; Probably","significato":"dynamite","termine_origine":"Dynamit","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Dynamit","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"δύναμις","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Probably borrowed from German Dynamit. Coined by Alfred Nobel, the inventor. Ultimately from Ancient Greek δύναμις (dúnamis, “power”) + -iet, possibly under the influence of dynamo or dynamisch."},{"parola":"fosfor","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"phosphorus","termine_origine":"Phosphor","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Phosphor","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"φωσφόρος","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from German Phosphor, from Ancient Greek φωσφόρος (phōsphóros, “light-bearing”)."},{"parola":"fysisch","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"physical, having to do with matter, nature, the material world","termine_origine":"physisch","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"physisch","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"φυσικός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from German physisch, ultimately from Ancient Greek φυσικός (phusikós), cognate with English physical, Malay fizikal."},{"parola":"gen","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"gene","termine_origine":"Gen","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Gen","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"γενεά","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"From German Gen, from Ancient Greek γενεά (geneá, “generation, descent”), from the aorist infinitive of γίγνομαι (gígnomai, “to come into being”). Coined by the Danish biologist Wilhelm Ludvig Johannsen in a German-language publication."},{"parola":"hellenisme","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"Hellenism","termine_origine":"Hellenismus","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Hellenismus","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"Ἑλληνισμός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from German Hellenismus, from Ancient Greek Ἑλληνισμός (Hellēnismós). Equivalent to Helleen + -isme."},{"parola":"hematoom","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motiv