om Ancient Greek λευκός (leukós, “white”) and αἷμα (haîma, “blood”)."},{"parola":"pyknisch","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"short and stocky in figure, mesomorphic","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"πυκνός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From German, which itself is from Ancient Greek πυκνός (puknós, “thick”). Cognate with English pyknic."},{"parola":"sceptisch","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"skeptical, sceptical","termine_origine":"skeptisch","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"skeptisch","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"σκεπτικός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From German skeptisch, a learned borrowing of Ancient Greek σκεπτικός (skeptikós, “thoughtful, inquiring”)."},{"parola":"skelet","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"skeleton (support structure of an organism; ensemble of animal bones)","termine_origine":"Skelett","catena":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Skelett","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"σκελετός","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*(s)kelh₁-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from German Skelett, from Ancient Greek σκελετός (skeletós, “dried up, withered, dried body, parched, mummy”), from σκελλώ (skellṓ, “to dry, dry up, to make dry, to parch”), from Proto-Indo-European *(s)kelh₁- (“to parch, wither”)."},{"parola":"stroboscoop","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"stroboscope","termine_origine":"Stroboskop","catena":[{"codi